maria: Heads-up: opened a PR to merge our 429/timeout/context-limit guidance into a single error-reference doc. Need snippets, a migration blurb, and a couple link fixes. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/495

alex: Nice. Quick note: the JS exponential backoff in the PR duplicates code in /snippets. Can we centralize to avoid divergence?

kevin: I can extract tiny retry helpers for JS and Python into /snippets. Proposal: show built-in SDK retry first, then an optional minimal wrapper. Example JS for docs:
```js
// Minimal backoff for docs only
async function withBackoff(fn, retries = 3) {
  let delay = 200;
  for (let i = 0; i < retries; i++) {
    try { return await fn(); } catch (e) { if (i === retries - 1) throw e; await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, delay)); delay *= 2; }
  }
}
```

maria: Perfect. CI is failing on a renamed anchor 'context-evict' -> 'context-eviction' causing a broken link.

